WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Christophe, well done. Woot Woot had just finished
second on a fast track — today, with the ground
softening, did that really help her?

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.200
No, that's not it. The other day, unfortunately,
she broke a bit slowly leaving the stalls,

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.200
and I found myself a long way off the lead.
They went at a hunting gallop and it was
sprinting hard up front,

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.400
and we were a bit caught out at the start.
She finished very, very well last time;

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.000
I think it was more a question of pace.
Today she broke very well — I found myself
straight in front and let her do her own thing,

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.000
and when I asked her to change legs and accelerate
150 meters from the post, she reacted very well —
she took it very easily.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.400
Did you think you'd win as easily today?

8
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.200
No, no, no — before the race we were aiming more
for second than the win. We thought the Irish filly
would be hard to beat,

9
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:48.200
and in the end she wasn't in the race at all;
we never saw her alongside us.
So I rode my race out in front,

10
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.200
the filly was breathing very well, she was super relaxed,
and when I asked her to change rhythm
she reacted very, very well.

11
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.050
Thank you.
